# Core Technical Components

## 1. Leakage-Safe Temporal Pipeline

BIRE uses a leakage-safe time-series pipeline designed around strict temporal integrity.

Features include:

* patient-level grouping
* chronological ordering
* future-safe rolling windows
* shifted temporal aggregation
* continuous deterioration labeling

This ensures the model never accesses future patient information during feature generation.

---

## 2. Temporal Physiological Intelligence

The system models physiological progression across time using:

* lag features
* rate-of-change (delta)
* rolling mean
* rolling standard deviation
* rolling minimum / maximum
* deterioration velocity
* trajectory spread
* convergence metrics

These features help identify:

* instability progression
* physiological drift
* deterioration acceleration
* escalation continuity

before hard thresholds are crossed.

---

## 3. Operational Risk Prediction

BIRE predicts deterioration using machine learning models trained on temporal physiological behavior.

Current modeling approaches include:

* Logistic Regression
* XGBoost
* LightGBM experimentation

The system predicts deterioration approximately:

> 60 minutes ahead

using 5-minute physiological intervals.

Evaluation focuses on:

* AUROC
* AUPRC
* lead-time analysis
* alert burden
* operational sensitivity
* episode continuity

---

# Gateway Suppression System (GSS)

One of BIRE’s core innovations is the:

> Gateway Suppression System (GSS)

GSS separates:

* risk prediction
* alert generation
* operational escalation

into distinct intelligence layers.

The suppression system is designed to reduce:

* alert fatigue
* repetitive alarms
* low-value notifications
* operational noise

while preserving meaningful escalation behavior.

GSS includes:

* persistence logic
* cooldown behavior
* suppression transparency
* escalation overrides
* timing-aware evaluation
* re-escalation continuity

---

# IBPIP — Personalized Baseline Intelligence

BIRE includes an adaptive baseline intelligence layer known as:

> IBPIP
> (Individualized Baseline & Personalized Intelligence Processing)

IBPIP explores:

* patient-specific baseline behavior
* long-term stability adaptation
* personalized monitoring context
* dynamic deterioration sensitivity

This layer allows BIRE to reason about deterioration relative to the patient’s own physiological behavior rather than only global thresholds.

---

# BIRE-FI — Forecasting Intelligence

BIRE-FI extends the system beyond static risk prediction into:

> operational forecasting intelligence.

The forecasting layer evaluates:

* deterioration directionality
* escalation probability
* trajectory acceleration
* monitoring continuity
* operational concern progression

Forecasting states include concepts such as:

* WATCH
* ESCALATE
* URGENT
* CRITICAL
* POST-EVENT MONITORING

